= Upper Silesia Partitioned

On 20 October the Allies accept the League of Nations' line through Upper Silesia. Germany keeps most of the land and most of the voters. Poland gets Kattowitz, Königshütte and most of the mines. The nationalist papers print black borders, and the mark falls again on the news. [? if spd_in_government = 1 : Wirth resigns in protest, and four days later forms a new cabinet, because nobody else will. ?]

- @ok: Very well.

@ok

The Rote Fahne writes that the miners of Kattowitz will be exploited in Polish by the same companies that exploited them in German.
